<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started"
  description="Start using llmdoc through its external dual-repository CLI, Claude Code plugin, Codex plugin, or a thin AGENTS.md recipe."
  section="getting-started"
>
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p>llmdoc requires Node.js 18 or newer and Git. The CLI is external tooling: do not add it to the repository you are working on. A knowledge base is a second, independent Git repository that is bound to your source repository.</p>

  <h2>Create and bind a knowledge repository</h2>
  <pre><code># Create an external knowledge repository and bind it to the source
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc init --source ./app --knowledge ../app-knowledge

# Or bind an existing independent knowledge repository
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc bind --source ./app --knowledge ../app-knowledge</code></pre>
  <p>The source repository is never modified. The knowledge repository is external by default; use <code>--nested</code> only when it must live inside the source worktree and the outer Git does not track that subtree.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>Always use the full scoped package name. A bare <code>npx llmdoc</code> resolves to an unrelated package.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Claude Code</h2>
  <p>Add the repository-verified marketplace, then install the plugin:</p>
  <pre><code>/plugin marketplace add https://github.com/TokenRollAI/llmdoc
/plugin install llmdoc@llmdoc-plugin</code></pre>
  <p>Once the plugin is active, initialize the repository with <code>/llmdoc:init</code>.</p>

  <h2>Codex</h2>
  <p>Add llmdoc as a plugin marketplace source, then install it from the Plugins Directory. Review the plugin hooks before trusting them.</p>
  <pre><code>codex plugin marketplace add TokenRollAI/llmdoc</code></pre>

  <h2>Other coding agents</h2>
  <p>Use a thin <code>AGENTS.md</code> rule that routes discovery through the external CLI. Keep durable knowledge in the independent Knowledge Git; never hand-edit <code>.llmdoc/meta.json</code>.</p>

  <h2>Your first retrieval</h2>
  <pre><code># Unclear scope
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc tree

# A concept or contract
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc search "retry policy"

# Context for concrete files
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc context --files src/api/client.ts</code></pre>
  <p>These are alternatives, not a mandatory sequence. Read document bodies with <code>show</code> only after identifying what matters.</p>

  <h2>Capture and publish</h2>
  <pre><code>npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc capture --title "retry budget" --from notes.md
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc update --promote inbox/retry-budget.md --to guides/retry.md \
  --kind guide --description "How retry budgets are chosen." --source-path "src/retry/**"
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc review
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc review --confirm &lt;reviewId&gt;
npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc commit --review &lt;reviewId&gt;</code></pre>
  <p>Publishing requires a valid source HEAD and a fully clean source worktree/index. A code change creates a review obligation; <code>delta</code> and <code>status</code> report what needs re-verification.</p>

  <h2>Browse locally</h2>
  <p>Launch the read-only viewer to inspect the fixed Knowledge HEAD. The server binds only to <code>127.0.0.1</code>.</p>
  <pre><code>npx -y @tokenroll/llmdoc serve</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
